<title>USA: Nalco Chemical authorizes share buyback.</title>
<headline>Nalco Chemical authorizes share buyback.</headline>
<dateline>NAPEREVILLE, Ill. 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nalco Chemical Co said Thursday its board had authorized a new stock repurchase plan under which the company can buy back three million shares.</p>
<p>It said all purchases authorized under prior plans have been made. The new plan continues the active buyback program started in 1992. Since then, Nalco has repurchased six million shares.  </p>
<p>Nalco has about 67 million shares of common outstanding, as well as about 394,000 shares of Series B ESOP convertible preferred stock, each convertible into 20 shares of common.</p>
<p>((-- Chicago Newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
